---
/**
 * PR 6b (R1) — the recipes property's OWN home.
 *
 * WHAT THIS IS
 * ------------
 * Until this page, `gustale.recipes/` served the ATLAS home: the same
 * `AtlasHeroKpi` band and the same `GustaleHomeIsland` workspace that
 * `gustale.com/` serves. ADR-007 recorded that as the problem R1 exists
 * to fix — "What gustale.recipes serves today is the same dish corpus,
 * re-framed". Two properties, one body of content, one presentation.
 *
 * R1 is "a minimal own home for the recipes property" (ADR-007, §"R1–R3
 * are, in order"). This is that minimal own home.
 *
 * WHAT IT IS NOT
 * --------------
 * It is NOT the per-dish recipe hub. That is item 5, it is a different
 * URL (`/dishes/<slug>` on the recipes origin), and it is built after
 * this one. The two are often confused because ADR §5.2 calls the
 * per-dish page "the hub"; here "the hub" means the recipes property's
 * own entry point, which is what the resume doc's task table and the
 * Nav both point at ("On the recipes domain 'Explore' is the recipes
 * home, which is the recipes LISTING — the site's entry point on this
 * domain").
 *
 * THE CONTRACT THIS PAGE KEEPS
 * ----------------------------
 * 1. It is a RECIPES page. It says so, and it does not pretend to be
 *    the Atlas. No Atlas history, places or families are copied here
 *    (ADR-007-A1 §5.3's "No history/places/families copied from the
 *    Atlas").
 * 2. It does NOT have "Add a dish" and does NOT link to `/dishes/new`.
 *    That control is the Atlas's (PR 6a, R3). "Add a recipe" is not
 *    offered either: there is no recipe to add until the schema and the
 *    API land (item 4), and offering a link to a form that does not
 *    exist is worse than offering nothing.
 * 3. It renders correctly and usefully with ZERO recipes — which is
 *    what every visitor sees today, because live has zero recipes. It
 *    does NOT fake content to look populated.
 * 4. It links to the Atlas for the thing the Atlas is for (history,
 *    origins, connections), and it links to the recipes listing for the
 *    thing this property is for (the recipes).
 */
import { atlasUrl, propertyName } from "../lib/domain";

// The recipes listing is this property's entry point for the recipes
// themselves. It is a recipes-domain route, so it is a local link.
const recipesHref = "/dishes";
// The Atlas dish, for a dish the reader wants the HISTORY of.
const atlasHref = atlasUrl("/dishes");

// The counts. They are the ATLAS's counts (dishes, places, families) —
// this page must not claim them as the recipes property's own numbers,
// so they are not fetched here. A count that belongs to the other
// property is not this page's to display.
//
// What this page CAN honestly count is the recipes, and that count is
// zero today. The API that would serve it (item 4) does not exist yet,
// so the page renders the zero it knows, in words, with an action
// attached — the rule the Atlas's own KPI band follows ("a zero belongs
// in an EMPTY STATE that has an action attached").

// "Add a recipe" is deliberately NOT offered: see the header note.
// The link to the authoring surface is only reachable once the recipe
// schema and its API exist (item 4). Offering a dead form is the
// defect R3 was about — so there is no authoring href here to keep
// alive, and no "Add a dish" control to inherit from the Atlas.
---

<section class="recipes-home" aria-labelledby="recipes-home-title">
  <div class="wrap">

    <p class="recipes-home__kicker">{propertyName()}</p>

    <h1 id="recipes-home-title" class="recipes-home__title">
      Recipes for the world's dishes.
    </h1>

    <p class="recipes-home__lede">
      The Atlas records where a dish came from — its history, its origins,
      its family, the connections it carries. This is the other half:
      <strong>how it is actually made</strong>. A recipe is one way of
      cooking a dish, with quantities, times, and a source for every
      claim it makes.
    </p>

    {/*
      THE EMPTY STATE — and today it is not an edge case.

      There are zero published recipes, because the recipe schema and
      its API are still being built (item 4). So this is what every
      visitor sees first, and it has to be worth reading on its own.

      It says three true things:
        * how many recipes there are (zero);
        * where the dish's history lives (the Atlas);
        * that the recipes are not here yet, without pretending they are.
    */}
    <div class="recipes-home__empty" role="status">
      <p class="recipes-home__count">
        <b>0</b>{" "}
        <span>published recipes</span>
      </p>
      <p class="recipes-home__emptynote">
        The recipe collection is being built. Nothing is here yet — so
        nothing is shown here yet. The dishes themselves are already
        documented on the Atlas.
      </p>
      <div class="recipes-home__emptyactions">
        <a href={atlasHref} class="btn-accent">
          Browse dishes on the Atlas ↗️
        </a>
        <a href={recipesHref} class="btn-ghost">
          See the recipe list →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/*
      WHAT THIS PROPERTY WILL HOLD.

      Three entries, each saying what it will be. They are not links to
      pages that do not exist: the only links here are to the recipes
      listing and to the Atlas. The rest is a statement of intent, which
      is honest and costs nothing.
    */}
    <div class="recipes-home__what">
      <h2 class="recipes-home__sectiontitle">What lands here</h2>
      <ul class="recipes-home__cards">
        <li class="recipes-home__card">
          <p class="recipes-home__cardnum">01</p>
          <h3 class="recipes-home__cardtitle">One recipe per variation</h3>
          <p class="recipes-home__cardbody">
            Nasi goreng kampung and nasi goreng jawa are two recipes, not
            one recipe with two names. Each carries its own quantities,
            times and method.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="recipes-home__card">
          <p class="recipes-home__cardnum">02</p>
          <h3 class="recipes-home__cardtitle">Every claim carries a source</h3>
          <p class="recipes-home__cardbody">
            A recipe is a set of claims about how to do something. An
            unsourced recipe looks authoritative, so every claim is
            sourced or marked as the contributor's own.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="recipes-home__card">
          <p class="recipes-home__cardnum">03</p>
          <h3 class="recipes-home__cardtitle">History stays on the Atlas</h3>
          <p class="recipes-home__cardbody">
            A recipe inherits its dish's identity — it does not duplicate
            it. Origins and history are not copied here; the Atlas keeps
            them, and each recipe links back.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    {/*
      THE CONTRIBUTION INVITATION.

      The Atlas is where a dish is documented; this is where a recipe is
      written. The one control that exists today is the Atlas's "Add a
      dish", and this page does not carry it — it points at the Atlas
      instead. That is the R3 rule: the recipes property stops
      promising a control it cannot deliver.

      When item 4 lands the recipe schema and its API, the "Write a
      recipe" control comes here and the link below becomes the recipe
      authoring surface. It is NOT in the markup now, and not behind a
      flag: a switch that is currently false is a promise the page
      cannot keep, and R3 was exactly about that.
    */}
    <div class="recipes-home__contribute">
      <h2 class="recipes-home__sectiontitle">Write a recipe</h2>
      <p class="recipes-home__contributelede">
        Recipes are added from the dish itself, and each one is reviewed
        before it goes live. Until that form exists, dishes are
        documented on the Atlas.
      </p>
      <a href={atlasHref} class="btn-ghost">
        Start with a dish on the Atlas ↗️
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* ── Page-local: the recipes home ─────────────────────────────────── */
  .recipes-home {
    padding: 56px 0 96px;
  }
  .recipes-home .wrap {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }

  .recipes-home__kicker {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 1.6px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .recipes-home__title {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5.5vw, 64px);
    line-height: 1.04;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .recipes-home__lede {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--sub);
    margin: 0 0 44px;
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  .recipes-home__lede strong {
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* ── The empty state ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .recipes-home__empty {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 34px 34px 36px;
    margin: 0 0 64px;
  }
  .recipes-home__count {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .recipes-home__count b {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 46px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .recipes-home__count span {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--sub);
  }
  .recipes-home__emptynote {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--sub);
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    max-width: 560px;
  }
  .recipes-home__emptyactions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .recipes-home__emptyactions .btn-accent,
  .recipes-home__emptyactions .btn-ghost,
  .recipes-home__contribute .btn-accent,
  .recipes-home__contribute .btn-ghost {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* ── "What lands here" ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .recipes-home__sectiontitle {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 1.6px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sub);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 26px;
  }
  .recipes-home__cards {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 64px;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .recipes-home__cards {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .recipes-home__cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .recipes-home__card {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 24px 22px 26px;
  }
  .recipes-home__cardnum {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .recipes-home__cardtitle {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .recipes-home__cardbody {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--sub);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Contribution ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .recipes-home__contribute {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 48px;
  }
  .recipes-home__contributelede {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--sub);
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    max-width: 560px;
  }
</style>
